+# Daily Grind
+
+The homepage loads `analytics.js` with `defer`. It queues a `page_view` on load
+(and when restored from the back/forward cache) and records clicks through one
+delegated listener without delaying navigation.
+
+Events are sent together after 500 ms without another event, after at most five
+seconds of continuous activity, or when the batch reaches 50 events. Hiding or
+leaving the page flushes any pending batch immediately. Delivery uses
+`navigator.sendBeacon`, falling back to a background `fetch` with `keepalive`.
+Failed delivery is dropped without retries to avoid extra traffic.
+
+Configure the destination using `data-endpoint` on the script in `index.html`.
+The default is `POST /api/analytics`; the hosting service must provide that
+endpoint (this repository only contains static files). It should accept JSON
+with this shape and return a successful response such as `204`:
+
+```json
+{
+  "events": [
+    { "type": "page_view", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T12:00:00.000Z", "path": "/" },
+    { "type": "click", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T12:00:00.100Z", "path": "/", "tag": "a", "destination": "/menu" }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+Click events include the nearest control's tag and, for HTTP(S) links, the
+destination pathname. No form values, page text, query strings, or fragments are
+collected. No cookies or persistent identifiers are created by the script.
